    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.trailspace\n\n### Description\n\nTo be consistent with the way the other plugins work, it should have a toggle function to show or hide highlight. (ex. MiniMap.toggle, MiniMisc.zoom ...). It would simplify adding keymap to the `\\` key which is the default toggle key of neovim. Right now, if I want to toggle the highlight, it's hard because I need to check if it's shown or hide and call the right function.",
