        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I'd generally agree with adding a separate `toggle`, in this particular case I'd like to keep 'mini.trailspace' minimal. It already is designed to show/hide trailspace only when needed. Customizing that is intended to be done via [manipulating `vim.{g,b}.minitrailspace_disable`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/dc1775613f672e6a804577945813353c5c4e6fe5/doc/mini-trailspace.txt#L35-L43) (which indeed might require an extra `highlight()` or `unhighlight()` call).\n\nClosing as not planned.\n\n------\n\n> It would simplify adding keymap to the `\\` key which is the default toggle key of neovim.\n\nJust FYI, but it is not the Neovim's default toggle key. By default it is a `<Leader>` key (see `:h mapleader`) and is repurposed as a default universal \"toggle\" prefix in ['mini.basics'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/dc1775613f672e6a804577945813353c5c4e6fe5/doc/mini-basics.txt#L97-L99).",
